 "text": "[curious] Pigeons brought news to besieged Paris. Balloons took them out. Prussia ringed Paris and cut the telegraph. Two million people were trapped. Only the sky was left. Balloons carried mail out. [tense] But balloons can't turn back. How would replies get in? Pigeons fly home from anywhere. So balloons carried them out. Birds can't carry letters. Photographer Dagron's trick: pages shrunk onto finger-sized film. The government sat in Tours. Dagron flew there to shrink letters. They tied the film to a pigeon's tail. In Paris, a screen enlarged the film. Clerks copied it. [somber] Most birds never returned. Still, tens of thousands of messages arrived. A secret message for Tours landed in Norway. The men lived, but it was out of Paris's hands. [warm] Man built balloons; wind steered them. Pigeons flew home with the news.",
